35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,The closeout files are telling. Some awards still draw users a decade later.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,I see. The mechanism-focused ones often ended with questions unresolved. That is a red flag.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The repository turnaround is now weeks, not years. That changes the calculus for data-heavy work.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The computing agreement is generous, but the animal-unit day rates have risen sharply. That is a hidden cost.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The staffing rolls show a shift. Fewer technicians, more modellers. The incident logs show idle time due to service gaps.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"Midori, the shift to modellers is interesting. Does that mean the bench work is less critical?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,Not necessarily. It means the risk profile has changed. I need to see who is actually available.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,The repository speed is a genuine advantage. It reduces the bottleneck for data-intensive proposals.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"The animal-unit cost is a significant variable. If a proposal relies heavily on that, the grant buys less.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"The idle time in the logs is concerning. It suggests that even if we fund the science, the infrastructure might not be ready.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree with Midori. Infrastructure readiness is a silent killer of good science.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,I am looking at the staffing rolls. I need to know if the trained hands are still here.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"The repository speed is a plus, but the animal-unit cost is a minus. We need to balance these.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The computing agreement is a plus, but the animal-unit cost is a minus. We need to balance these.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,The incident logs show that service gaps are a real risk. We should ask about maintenance plans.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
